# Prettier's ignore list. The rule for adding to it: a path belongs here when
# reformatting it would break something, not merely when nobody has formatted
# it yet.

node_modules/
yarn.lock

# GENERATED BINDINGS. scripts/generated-paths.txt is this repository's single
# definition of "generated", and gate:drift regenerates every entry there and
# requires a byte-for-byte empty diff against what is committed. Prettier does
# not know that: `prettier --write` reformats these files perfectly happily,
# and the next `yarn gate:drift` then fails on a diff whose only cause is the
# formatter. Measured 2026-09-02 -- a single pass rewrote 3113 lines of
# src/generated/matrix_crypto.ts and 21 of src/index.tsx.
#
# Listed by hand rather than read from generated-paths.txt, because
# .prettierignore is a static file with no include mechanism. The four entries
# omitted here (cpp/generated, android, ios, MatrixCrypto.podspec) hold nothing
# Prettier has a parser for.
packages/react-native-matrix-crypto/src/generated/
packages/react-native-matrix-crypto/src/index.tsx
packages/react-native-matrix-crypto/src/NativeMatrixCrypto.ts

# Build outputs and vendored trees, all of them already in .gitignore. Naming
# them again is what keeps `yarn format` from walking a working copy that has
# actually built something.
rust/target/
build/
**/build/
**/Pods/
api-docs/
*.xcframework/

# Machine-written and re-written on every measurement run, by
# scripts/measure-artifacts.sh. It happens to emit exactly what Prettier would
# (`JSON.stringify(all, null, 2) + '\n'`), so this is not currently load-
# bearing -- it is here so that a change to that script's output cannot start
# a fight between the script and the formatter that neither side loses.
artifact-sizes.json

# The React Native template's native projects for the example app. Xcode and
# Android Studio write files in here (asset catalogues, `Contents.json`,
# generated Gradle bits) in their own formats and rewrite them on their own
# schedule; a formatter fighting an IDE over those is churn with no reader.
packages/example-app/ios/
packages/example-app/android/

# THE TYPE TEST'S LINE STRUCTURE IS THE TEST. Eleven `@ts-expect-error`
# directives in this file each apply to the line that follows them, and the
# assertions they guard are single-line object literals. Prettier breaks those
# literals across lines, which moves the error the compiler reports onto an
# inner line -- so the directive above it becomes "Unused '@ts-expect-error'
# directive" (TS2578) AND the error it was there to absorb becomes real.
# Measured 2026-09-02: one `prettier --write` turned a clean `tsc --noEmit`
# into six errors, three of each kind, and every one of them named a line
# whose code had not changed.
#
# The narrower fix is a `// prettier-ignore` above each of the five literals,
# and it was not taken: the next `@ts-expect-error` written here would need a
# sixth, nothing would ask for it, and the failure it causes reads as a broken
# assertion rather than as a formatter. The file is a sheet of compile-time
# assertions that is never executed; there is nothing here for a formatter to
# make more readable that is worth that trap.
packages/react-native-matrix-crypto/src/types.type-test.ts
